<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Franco denies rumor of new global bond.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Franco denies rumor of new global bond.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil has no plans to launch a new global bond, contrary to rumors in markets, Central Bank International Affairs director Gustavo Franco said.</p>
<p>Franco said rumors of a new global debt issue by Brazil tended to surface every time markets felt conditions for such an issue were right.</p>
<p>Brazil, which launched a $750 million global bond in October, might place small amounts of debt in various markets and currencies, but had no immediate plans for another global issue, he said.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
